## The list

Select **People** under **Clients**. The page is titled **Contacts** and lists the people your firm deals with: directors, shareholders, contact persons and others. The columns are **Full name**, **Nationality**, **Residency** (Citizen, PR, EP or Non-resident), **Email**, **Phone** and **Status** (Active or Archived). Search by name in the box at the top.

## Add a person

{% steps %}
1. Select **+ New Contact**. The **New contact** dialog opens.
2. Type the **Full name**. **Known as**, **Nationality**, **Residency**, **Email**, **Phone** and **Notes** are optional.
3. Under **Identity check (optional)**, choose the document type (NRIC, FIN, Passport or address proof) and type the ID number. If the person is already on file, the dialog shows the existing record with the ID masked; select **Open existing** instead of creating a duplicate.
4. Select **Create**.
{% /steps %}

You can also add a person while adding a role at a company (see [Relationships](/en/clients/relationships/#add-a-role)).

## The person page

Select a person to open their page. The tabs are:

| Tab | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Details** | **Contact info** — name, title, nationality, e-mail, phone, WeChat, preferred language, residency, address, notes and tags — and **Contact cards**: the person's contact details for each company they work with. **Make primary** marks the main card. |
| **Timeline** | Notes, cases and documents about the person. |
| **Activity** | Changes to the person's details. |
| **Cases** | Cases for the person. |
| **Companies** | The companies where the person holds a role, with **Add company** to add one, and related people (spouse, relative, friend). |
| **Services** | Services from contracts billed to the person. |
| **Invoices** | Invoices for the person. |

**New opportunity** at the top starts a CRM opportunity for the person.

Identity numbers (NRIC, FIN, passport) are never shown in full.

A person cannot be deleted from the person page. A person who was linked only to a company that has ended service with a struck-off date is archived automatically (see [End or restore service](/en/clients/end-service/)).
